/* Thrones module: 06-endgame-throne.partial.if */
scene__
  @name "ACT6: Throne Calculus"
  @first "T409 - ACT6 - The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
  @sections "T409 - ACT6 - The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke" "T410 - ACT6 - Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog" "T411 - ACT6 - Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood" "T412 - ACT6 - The Wall War Map against old law" "T413 - ACT6 - Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky" "T414 - ACT6 - Moat Cailin Whispered Warning at the gatehouse" "T415 - ACT6 - Oldtown Silent Betrayal behind closed doors" "T416 - ACT6 - Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower" "T417 - ACT6 - Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow" "T418 - ACT6 - Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn" "T419 - ACT6 - The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain" "T420 - ACT6 - Riverrun Broken Oath under rain"
__scene

section__
  @title "T409 - ACT6 - The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-throne/frame-409.jpg"

  "The Eyrie map chamber is colder than the battlefields you just left. Wax smoke curls above casualty ledgers while scribes sharpen fresh quills for a war that now happens in signatures instead of charges. Tyrion Lannister insists the realm needs an explicit succession framework before another banner defects. Daenerys watches in silence, measuring whether your law serves order or merely cloaks fear.

Neutral lords no longer ask who won the sieges. They ask who can guarantee roads, courts, and grain convoys through winter. A public settlement can bind rivals to visible obligations and expose every concession as weakness. A covert settlement can secure immediate obedience through debt, hostages, and blackmail while sowing the very resentments that end dynasties.

Outside, high winds rattle the shutters like dice in a cup. The first decree of the new order will decide what sort of throne can survive the second decree."

  choice__
    @target "T410 - ACT6 - Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action crown_trust = clampStat(crown_trust + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Convene a witnessed succession court and bind claimants to written constitutional terms before the realm."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T411 - ACT6 - Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 2, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Build a private patronage bloc through hostages, debt notes, and deniable leverage over key electors."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T410 - ACT6 - Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-throne/frame-410.jpg"

  "On the Iron Throne dais, hammered metal still smells of blood and lamp oil. Sansa Stark demands enforceable limits on crown requisitions before the north commits another winter levy. Varys brings reports that captains are abandoning garrisons because no one trusts which proclamations are real. Claimant houses crowd the galleries, ready to call any delay proof of illegitimacy.

Succession is now an operational problem as much as a moral one. If command law is public and legible, armies hold formation and rivals gain material to contest each clause. If command law is private and coercive, you can move faster while teaching every officer to obey fear over institutions. A third path can import outside guarantors and money, but at the price of sovereignty.

The throne room echoes with boots, steel, and whispered arithmetic. Every party here is counting what your settlement will cost them before they decide whether to honor it."

  choice__
    @target "T411 - ACT6 - Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action crown_trust = clampStat(crown_trust + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Read a formal command charter before assembled houses, forcing military loyalty into public law."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T412 - ACT6 - The Wall War Map against old law"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 7)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 2, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Whip support through sealed bargains and private kompromat, securing votes before opposition can organize."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T413 - ACT6 - Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky"
    @when ((wealth + essos_ties + dragon_factor) >= 7)
    @action wealth = clampStat(wealth - 1, 0, 30)
    @action dragon_factor = clampStat(dragon_factor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action essos_ties = clampStat(essos_ties + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Buy Pentoshi credit and neutral guarantors to force a rapid settlement, trading coin for outside influence."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T411 - ACT6 - Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-throne/frame-411.jpg"

  "In the king's solar, foreign envoys from Qarth and Pentos wait beside hostages who are supposed to guarantee their contracts. Varys warns that each envoy has already promised different terms to different claimants. Sansa points out the obvious: if foreign guarantees become the true source of legitimacy, every Westerosi oath becomes negotiable credit.

You can formalize these alliances in open record and force outside actors to accept scrutiny. That stabilizes commerce while exposing how dependent the crown has become on external lenders and shipping houses. Or you can keep the terms fragmented and secret, preserving tactical flexibility while ensuring the next succession crisis begins with financial blackmail and disputed obligations.

Rain strikes the casement glass in hard bursts. Somewhere below, a hostage child is crying, and no one in this room pretends not to hear it."

  choice__
    @target "T412 - ACT6 - The Wall War Map against old law"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action crown_trust = clampStat(crown_trust + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Publish one foreign-alliance register and enforce identical terms across houses, accepting immediate backlash."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T413 - ACT6 - Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 2, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Maintain parallel secret deals with rival envoys, preserving leverage now and banking future coercion."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T412 - ACT6 - The Wall War Map against old law"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-throne/frame-412.jpg"

  "The White Sword Tower smells of oiled steel and wet parchment. Daenerys presses for a decisive settlement that discourages rebellion through unmistakable strength. Tyrion argues that if crown policy ignores the Wall again, no throne settlement matters because the realm it governs may not survive the season. Crown guards pass altered raven copies from hand to hand, each with different claims of what you already decided.

This is the fault line between spectacle and survival. A public frontier compact can yoke succession legitimacy to northern defense and make southern elites pay visible costs. A covert pressure campaign can move supplies faster by bypassing debate, while convincing half the realm that governance now means manipulated terror. Either path defines what authority will look like under the next crown.

The map table is pinned with black stones for dead keeps and white stones for those still holding. There are fewer white stones every week."

  choice__
    @target "T413 - ACT6 - Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action crown_trust = clampStat(crown_trust + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Bind the new succession deal to a witnessed Wall-defense compact with mandatory grain and troop quotas."
  __choice

