section__
  @title "T413 - ACT6 - Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-throne/frame-413.jpg"

  "Castle Black's inheritance gallery is crowded with faith delegates, quartermasters, and survivors who carried the war on their backs. Tyrion presents a draft charter for command inheritance if northern lords fall. Daenerys questions whether concessions to distant garrisons will hollow the capital at the moment of coronation. Grain clerks have already begun rationing by political reliability, and everyone sees it.

Granting northern guarantees in open law can stabilize military confidence while reducing your bargaining room with southern claimants. Quietly extracting concessions from weaker factions can protect central control, but it transforms every promise into suspected extortion. You can also buy outside logistics support and force a temporary solution, though every foreign convoy arrives with policy strings attached.

Snow presses against the leaded windows, muting the hall. The people gathered here have heard too many promises and buried too many men to accept another vague one."

  choice__
