section__
  @title "T414 - ACT6 - Moat Cailin Whispered Warning at the gatehouse"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-throne/frame-414.jpg"

  "At Moat Cailin, rain drums on slate while messengers crowd the gatehouse with contradictory oaths from the same banner houses. Sansa insists that only an open reckoning can end the rumor war before coronation. Varys quietly shows you names of officers paid to stage defections if settlement terms become too restrictive. The line between intelligence and provocation is now almost invisible.

One faction threatens to break by sunrise unless you prove who actually commands the crossings. A public process can reestablish shared rules and embarrass allies you still need. A covert manipulation can collapse the dissent network overnight while validating every fear that the new regime is built on hidden knives. Both options move you forward. Neither leaves everyone loyal.

Mud from a hundred boots has turned the floor black. These are the last hours where allegiance can still be negotiated instead of imposed."

  choice__
