section__
  @title "T415 - ACT6 - Oldtown Silent Betrayal behind closed doors"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-throne/frame-415.jpg"

  "Oldtown's sealed records chamber smells of ink, mold, and sea wind. Varys lays out correspondence proving maesters, guilds, and sept officials have each drafted different legal justifications for who should rule. Sansa notes that if every faction can quote a different precedent, the first coronation decree will be challenged before the crown cools.

Neutral houses now wait to commit grain and coin until they see whether your settlement is rule-bound or merely expedient. A public legal settlement can establish coherent legitimacy and strip you of private bargaining tools. A covert settlement can buy immediate compliance through secret guarantees and make every future dispute a blackmail market. You can also use foreign financing to enforce outcomes quickly, at the cost of domestic credibility.

The bells of Oldtown carry through the shutters in slow intervals. Each one sounds like a deadline the realm can no longer postpone."

