section__
  @title "T416 - ACT6 - Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-throne/frame-416.jpg"

  "At Pyke's broken tower, surf smashes the rocks below and sprays salt across your treaty table. Daenerys demands a hard line against houses still testing your authority by withholding hostages. Tyrion counters that another round of exemplary brutality may win the week and destroy the coalition needed to survive winter. Foreign envoys in the gallery are already pricing which claimants might replace you.

Desertion reports from western garrisons show the same pattern: officers flee when succession terms seem reversible. A public hostage settlement can signal institutional finality and stop the drift. A covert settlement can neutralize immediate threats through disappearances and deniable swaps, but it converts every ally into a potential revenge plot. This is where your method becomes your regime.

Salt has blurred half the signatures on yesterday's draft. The sea is erasing indecision faster than your scribes can rewrite it."

  choice__
