section__
  @title "T418 - ACT6 - Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-throne/frame-418.jpg"

  "In Sunspear's prison gallery, a captured intermediary confesses to coordinating forged decrees between rival councils. Sansa demands the confession be tested before witnesses so no side can dismiss it as theater. Varys warns that if the network is not broken before the coronation, every order you issue in the first month can be spoofed and weaponized.

This is the final intelligence bottleneck before the settlement closes. Public adjudication can restore trust in records and permanently shame powerful accomplices. Quiet resolution can remove the network faster and keep fragile allies from bolting, while guaranteeing that conspiracy becomes your default administrative tool. Either choice will be remembered as the true constitution beneath the one you sign.

Dust motes drift through angled light onto shackles bolted in the floor. The room is built to hold bodies, but tonight it is holding the future of your paperwork."

  choice__
    @target "T419 - ACT6 - The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action crown_trust = clampStat(crown_trust + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Put the conspiracy confession to open inquiry and codify evidentiary rules for crown decrees."
  __choice

